Insert all into a set. For each num, expand only if num-1 is not in the set (start of a sequence).

```python
def longest_consecutive(nums):
    s = set(nums)
    best = 0
    for n in s:
        if n - 1 not in s:
            length = 0
            while n + length in s:
                length += 1
            best = max(best, length)
    return best
```

